{%- comment -%}
  EVERSTORY — buy-box note for the studio-laid-out sheet (Name & Photo Sticker Sheet).
  A product is a pack when custom.pack_sizes is set. Packs have no Size option:
  the size mix is fixed and the studio sizes each photo.
  2026-09-24 (owner: "too wordy, hard to follow"): the Sizes / Photos / Name paragraphs
  repeated what each field's own hint and the accordions below already say, and sat
  between Material and the first field. Now one line under the material photo; the
  template skips its Material paragraph for packs. Details live in the accordions
  (What you get, Materials, Sizes).
  2026-09-25 (owner: "not needed"): the last line went too, so packs show nothing here.
  The es_choice_helper custom-liquid block that renders this snippet is a bare <div> in
  the product details' 24px-gap flex column — left empty it would still add a gap, so the
  marker hides that block's wrapper (:has — older browsers just keep the extra gap). Each marker has
  its own value and its rule matches only that value: es-how-to-order uses the same trick one level
  up, and a shared marker let this two-level rule hide the whole product details column (2026-09-25).
  Renders nothing on products without pack_sizes (Custom Sticker Sheet, legacy
  products), so it is safe to place on the shared product template.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign pack_sizes = product.metafields.custom.pack_sizes.value -%}
{%- if pack_sizes != blank -%}
  <span data-es-empty-block="choice-helper" hidden></span>
  <style>
    div:has(> div > [data-es-empty-block='choice-helper']) {
      display: none;
    }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}
